 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Delivery via self-hosted WebSockets.** Committed changes are pushed over WebSockets to avoid realtime vendor coupling. Five-second HTTPS polling was rejected for repeated reads and lag; hosted realtime service was rejected for recurring fees and provider coupling. The choice accepts connection capacity and reconnect operational work in exchange for fast updates and vendor independence. See `docs/decisions/delivery-approach-self-hosted-websockets.md`.
